Read a cell from the primary screen while the alternate is up

A copy of the terminal made elsewhere -- BeerSSH's server keeps one and
sends it to a client that reconnects (its project.md sec 5.6) -- has to
carry the screen a full-screen program is drawn over, or leaving the
program shows the client whatever it had before. vterm_screen_get_cell()
reads only the screen showing, and the buffers are private to screen.c.

vterm_screen_get_primary_cell() is the same read from the primary buffer,
with the same conversion, swapping the buffer in for the one call.

---
--- a/include/vterm.h
+++ b/include/vterm.h
@@ -625,6 +625,9 @@
 int vterm_screen_get_attrs_extent(const VTermScreen *screen, VTermRect *extent, VTermPos pos, VTermAttrMask attrs);
 
 int vterm_screen_get_cell(const VTermScreen *screen, VTermPos pos, VTermScreenCell *cell);
+/* The same, from the primary screen whichever one is showing: what is under
+ * a full-screen program, for a copy of the terminal made elsewhere. */
+int vterm_screen_get_primary_cell(const VTermScreen *screen, VTermPos pos, VTermScreenCell *cell);
 
 int vterm_screen_is_eol(const VTermScreen *screen, VTermPos pos);
 
--- a/src/screen.c
+++ b/src/screen.c
@@ -1371,6 +1371,19 @@
   return 1;
 }
 
+/* Read with the primary buffer swapped in for the one call: getcell() and
+ * screencell_to_cell() read the current buffer, and are the conversion the
+ * screen's own cells get. Nothing else can run between the two swaps. */
+int vterm_screen_get_primary_cell(const VTermScreen *screen, VTermPos pos, VTermScreenCell *cell)
+{
+  VTermScreen *writable = (VTermScreen *)screen;
+  ScreenCell *showing = writable->buffer;
+  writable->buffer = writable->buffers[BUFIDX_PRIMARY];
+  int got = vterm_screen_get_cell(screen, pos, cell);
+  writable->buffer = showing;
+  return got;
+}
